@*
    The Desk's half of <head>: the theme boot script and the stylesheets, in the one order that
    works. A consumer puts <DeskHead /> in its App.razor head and its own sheets after it.

    Order is load-bearing. The stored theme is stamped on <html> first, before any stylesheet
    paints — ThemeService cannot until the circuit opens. A classic script, not a module, so it
    blocks for that one job. Then MudBlazor, so it can be overridden; desk.css next, because it
    defines the tokens; controls.css straight after the file whose tokens it spends; themes.css
    after those, because its token blocks tie with :root on specificity and win on source order;
    mud-bridge.css after that, because it spends the tokens on MudBlazor's variables and
    out-specifies what MudBlazor hard-codes. The application's own stylesheet comes after this
    component: it holds its windows, spends the Desk's tokens, and wins a tie with any Desk rule
    on source order.
*@
<script src="@Assets[DeskAssets.Js("theme-boot.js")]"></script>
@*  The regular face is on every page, and desk.css names it only once the sheet has arrived and
    parsed, so without this the font is the last request the head makes and the first paint is in
    the fallback. The italic is set in two places and loads when one of them draws.

    The one link here not through @Assets, on purpose. A preload is only used if it is the
    request the @font-face makes, and desk.css asks for the plain path — a stylesheet's url() is
    not fingerprinted — so a fingerprinted preload would be a second download of the same file.
    crossorigin because a font is always fetched in CORS mode; without it the preload is a
    different request again. *@
<link rel="preload" href="@(DeskAssets.Root + "/fonts/InterVariable.woff2")" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["_content/MudBlazor/MudBlazor.min.css"]" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets[DeskAssets.Css("desk.css")]" />
@* The newer primitives (menus, popovers) — straight after the file whose tokens they spend. *@
<link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets[DeskAssets.Css("controls.css")]" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets[DeskAssets.Css("themes.css")]" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets[DeskAssets.Css("mud-bridge.css")]" />
